From 1b637ed1e7128789419a06d46d62a7f044a46a02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lab(#53 Q1-C): bounded admission on top of priority-aware
 eviction

A decode job now starts only if strictly less useful (or unwanted)
decoded images free enough room; otherwise it evicts nothing and waits.
Equally useful work no longer swaps places, which was the at-rest
decode/evict cycle (lab probe: ~33 decodes/s at rest, zero network).

- Deferred jobs keep their asset compressed via the existing idle warm
  path, so admission later costs a decode, not a fetch.
- Deferred work is reconsidered only when demand changes (retain/pin with
  a different set or priorities) or capacity changes (a job finishes):
  identical per-frame retain/pin calls no longer re-run admission.
- stats(): deferred, admissionPasses.

Regression checks in sequence-contracts (#53 Q1): wanted bytes over the
budget, low priority displacing useful images, forward/reverse scroll
priorities, deferred dedupe/stale/compressed/resolve, identical demand,
and decoded + reserved <= budget sampled every 1 ms. The existing detail
serialization check now expects the over-budget equal-priority remainder
to wait (intentional behaviour change). The fetch fixture accepts a
missing init, as the warm path calls fetch(url).

Q1 arm C for Quackles Lab, on top of 99a629f9 (B) and 6f2ef5d2 (W1).
Not for promotion.

